  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "DeciLM checkpoints need per-block attention and FFN descriptions rather than Llama's uniform KV-head count and intermediate width. The change registers DeciLMForCausalLM and adds dedicated configuration and model classes.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_27a64ff1db314344b4d52bd58b3f31df",
          "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
          "call_5bcaffd8d1864a229bb451964edbbb77"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Reusing Attention, GatedMLP and TransformerBlock keeps the existing execution machinery while allowing checkpoint layer numbering, active cache numbering and FFN widths to differ.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
          "call_11471df83aff4338b138ee66be5cab06",
          "call_43e0ce5502024ab3bf00b1ae169e958c"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Config.from_directory can now dispatch DeciLMForCausalLM to DeciLMConfig; Model.from_config subsequently instantiates DeciLMModel. Registration does not imply compatibility with every Nemotron configuration.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_27a64ff1db314344b4d52bd58b3f31df",
          "call_4b986ee963c04e4c827cb8f0f8bf272e",
          "call_93913323ecf1489eaa94e1ab663b1780",
          "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The earlier optional-branch entry records missing-normalization and empty-allocation hazards in TransformerBlock.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_d48a48470ebc4aa286196a742309719f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Those implementations are unchanged here. DeciLM supplies a norm whenever its corresponding branch exists, avoiding the missing-normalization trigger. It can construct entirely empty blocks; conversion skips their allocation, but its later bitrate calculation has a separate zero-denominator hazard.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
          "call_0b73e7b306a44e08b08bdad3c5924a8b",
          "call_e19d110e1a8e4190b538a614e7a52fca",
          "call_62ccdaacccb248668cb1cc6a8e4b8604"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The inspected discussions report different problems: issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d concerns native-extension loading; issue #12, \u201cQwen2.5 Coder 0.5B Instruct | ValueError: Unsupported type in stop_conditions,\u201d concerns chat invocation; PR #13, \u201cFix a tokenizer issue while converting models without a bos_token_id defined,\u201d concerns null BOS handling. None supplies DeciLM execution evidence.",
        "basis": "source",
