    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Construct DeciLM from heterogeneous block descriptions",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "DeciLMConfig requires block_configs to have num_hidden_layers entries. It reads global hidden size and query-head count, derives head_dim by integer division when absent or false, accepts SiLU or an omitted activation declaration, and uses the existing NEOX-style RoPE settings reader. Unlike LlamaConfig, it does not require a global intermediate_size or num_key_value_heads.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_4b986ee963c04e4c827cb8f0f8bf272e",
              "call_5bcaffd8d1864a229bb451964edbbb77"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each block reads attention and ffn dictionaries. A truthy no_op removes that branch and its norm. Active attention maps n_heads_in_group directly to num_kv_heads and uses separate q_proj, k_proj, v_proj and o_proj tensors. Active FFNs use gate_proj, up_proj and down_proj through GatedMLP's default SiLU activation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_11471df83aff4338b138ee66be5cab06",
              "call_43e0ce5502024ab3bf00b1ae169e958c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "FFN width is int(2 \u00d7 ffn_mult \u00d7 hidden_size / 3), then rounded upward to a multiple of 256 using (width + 255) // 256 \u00d7 256. Here 255 is the rounding offset, not a separate size limit.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library transcription produced head_dim=128 for both 8192/64 and 16384/128. At hidden size 8192, multipliers 0.5, 1, 1.3125, 2.625, 3.28125 and 5.25 produce widths 2816, 5632, 7168, 14336, 17920 and 28672. At hidden size 16384, multiplier 0.4875 produces 5376 and multiplier 39 produces 425984.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_48aafba953b244df81e1a87475e6f559"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Tensor names retain the original block index, while cache_layer_idx advances only for active attention. This matches Attention.decode_flash_attn's lookup by layer_idx and Model.get_cache_layers' traversal of KV-capable modules. last_kv_module_idx records the last attention-bearing top-level block, allowing Model.prefill to stop there rather than execute trailing FFN-only blocks.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_11471df83aff4338b138ee66be5cab06",
              "call_93913323ecf1489eaa94e1ab663b1780"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The model retains token embedding, final RMSNorm and logits projection. Tied embeddings have an alternate-key path when the primary head is absent. prepare_inputs stores input_ids and delegates to prepare_for_attn, whose default is uncached Flash Attention; cached execution still requires its existing cache and position metadata.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_11471df83aff4338b138ee66be5cab06"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Active branches explicitly reject linear replacement and sparsification. Active attention also rejects sink-token and related sink-attention options. These checks occur after the no_op test, so disabled branches need neither valid projection dimensions nor supported active-branch options.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned nvidia/Llama-3_3-Nemotron-Super-49B-v1 configuration uses 80 layers, hidden size 8192, 64 query heads and eight KV heads for active attention. Its disabled attention branches and varying FFN multipliers fit the new construction choices; all FFNs remain active and the explicitly rejected options are false or null. It declares SiLU, untied embeddings and Llama-3 RoPE scaling with factor 8, so those values are supplied rather than inferred from defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_f3e2de7843994aeea4a1e5f11b2eb115",
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-51B-Instruct configuration also uses 80 layers, hidden size 8192, 64 query heads, SiLU, untied embeddings and RoPE factor 8. Its ordinary attention and FFN descriptions map to the new fields, but active replace_with_linear attention makes the model incompatible with the constructor's explicit assertion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4ae5082d9a454c6186f17df475f1603b",
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-CPT-v1 configuration uses 162 layers, hidden size 16384, 128 query heads and 16 KV heads for active attention, with SiLU, untied embeddings and RoPE factor 16. Its active-branch options fit the checks, but it contains fully disabled blocks that expose the conversion hazard recorded here.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_02aab2b62eaa4009a3593fcf81031b44",
              "call_6adc32af8d3d47258d5ded12f9424656",
              "call_b4ac408fd9a34b6bb14e1db10f05d947",
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_62ccdaacccb248668cb1cc6a8e4b8604"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The pinned nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-v1 configuration independently has the same listed global dimensions, active KV-head count, activation, untied embeddings and RoPE factor as the CPT variant. Its branch descriptions likewise include fully disabled blocks; registration and configuration parsing therefore do not establish successful conversion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5a79634e0eba4ace92df2b8b73d6bc39",
              "call_89a60826ca1a4f67844be4c251048979",
              "call_c0b1583ac6ad42b68753481ba3e3ce78",
              "call_658db52e7e464e96a481fe6114fa6d7b",
              "call_62ccdaacccb248668cb1cc6a8e4b8604"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
